  "body": "### What is the issue with the Test Utils Standard?\n\nThere is currently no way to simulate clicking notification, so the test coverage of notification is limited.\n\nI suggest a new function in testutils, because it doesn't seem possible that we can do this via webdriver - a tagless notification only has an internal identifier (at least in Gecko), and thus webdriver has no good way to identify a notification to request a click simulation (unless we also expose another webdriver command to enumerate notifications with their internal identifiers). But if we have a webidl test function, the function can extract the identifier right from a notification object.\n\nThoughts? @annevk ",
